nd in Sun because that's just how the  bolsa construction company rolls  the first guy you need is a strong goron  by the name of Grayson he's hanging out  in the southern mine in the Eldon region  so talk to him and he'll be ecstatic to  join Hudson's crew head back to  Tarrytown and Hudson will request even  more wood if you're having trouble  chopping down trees head to any stable  and you'll typically find an axe perfect  for your lumberjacking needs  you'll also need to find them another  worker and this time you'll want to  recruit ronson a Gerudo she's over right  here you'll repeat this process again  for the retail worker bison and finally  round out the troop with a Zora priest  named captain it'll all culminate in a  wonderful little wedding ceremony for  Hudson but your efforts will be rewarded  with more than just a ribbon to cut and  some rice itas a traveler by the name of  grant a will stop by the completed town  and if you talk to him he'll offer to  sell you pieces of rare high-level gear  granted you've already discovered it so  if he found a piece of barbarian armor  you can actually visit grant a and buy  the remaining two pieces from him and a  someone unreasonable price also if you  manage somehow to break your really nice  weapons such as the Hylian Shield you  can buy that back from him as well it's  a little expensive so don't go around  shield surfing on it all the time unless  you enjoy coughing up several thousand  rupees each time it breaks and there you  have it getting a house in breath of the  wild is as simple as chopping down a  tree selling some more and finding a  priest to Wed the form into a Gerudo  trust me it's a lot easier than it  sounds but if you enjoyed this guide  please subscribe to the gamespot youtube  channel so you can keep up with all the  latest breath of the wild videos

